(3) THE LATTICE THRESHOLD w* = B*sum(core): beyond it, no SHORT new relation.
    Relation t.(core+[w])=0, t_w!=0 => |t_w| w = |sum core t_i v_i| <= B*sum(core)
    for |t_i|<=B. So w>B*sum(core) forces t_w=0 for all |t_i|<=B.
================================================================================

  core12 sum = 85
    B  w*=B*sum   min |s| at t=B+1 (7-coprime)
    1        85                       0.124432
    2       170                       0.103443
    3       255                       0.077582
    6       510                       0.017264
   12      1020                       0.010624
   20      1700                       0.006278

  For w beyond w*(B), the relation lattice of core∪{w} equals Lambda(core)
  (t_w=0) plus relations with ALL core coeffs > B. Their theta s-products are
  <= (max|s| beyond B)^(#nonzero) -> 0 as B->inf, giving L(core∪w)->(6/7)L(core).

  numeric: w=1036 (mult of 14, > w*(B=12)=1020):
     L(core12 ∪ 1036) = 0.00705536  vs (6/7)L0 = 0.00699301  (|err|=6.24e-05)

