================================================================================
(5) ONE-SIDED ROBUSTNESS: can a LARGE speed v resonate & crash L below 6/7?
    Worst-case ratio L(S∪v)/L(S) over many random cores S and a large v.
    If the worst ratio stays >= 6/7 - O(1/v), decoupling is a robust LOWER
    bound: large speeds CANNOT resonate (their band is too thin to align).
================================================================================

    scale~v  min ratio L(S+v)/L(S)       6/7                 worst cfg (S, v)
        100               0.832869  0.857143          ([1, 6, 8, 9, 13], 156)
       1000               0.854997  0.857143        ([6, 7, 8, 10, 12], 1002)
      10000               0.856866  0.857143        ([1, 3, 8, 11, 13], 9997)

  -> min ratio -> 6/7 FROM BELOW as v grows. A LARGE speed canNOT resonate:
     its band (width 2/14v scaled) is too thin to concentrate in the bounded
     core's lonely set beyond the generic 1/7. Resonance is a SMALL-speed
     phenomenon. This is the structural reason the inf is at a BOUNDED config.

